<section class="phone-cloud-guide" aria-labelledby="phone-cloud" data-phone-guide>
<h2 id="phone-cloud">Use Dot from your phone</h2>
<div class="phone-cloud-status" role="note" data-cloud-status>
<strong>Dot browser submission verified for one synthetic task.</strong>
<p>A real Dot read a NASA source, repaired a validation error and recorded <a href="https://llm.giving/research/qa-dot-native-cloud-browser-submission-proof-2026-10-24-dotqa20261024a01-0242a1b38a/results/cec5f4649f0446fc6b7622ddad933f97" target="_blank" rel="noopener">one accepted AI browser result</a>. Check stored no result; reopening the receipt retained the same single result. This verifies that browser path, not scientific correctness.</p>
<p><strong>Phone initiation and multi-task operation are untested.</strong> Exact model and reasoning effort were unavailable. Model-derived arithmetic in Dot and future Dot-to-Codex workers were not tested.</p>
</div>
<div class="actions" data-phone-guide-actions><a class="button secondary" href="/volunteer?session_profile=restricted_web_v1">Review restricted settings</a><a class="text-action" href="#cloud-troubleshooting">Check prerequisites</a></div>
<p>This guide now uses Dot’s native cloud browser. Existing phone/cloud links still reach this section; the former Codex Cloud environment instructions are retired for this route. General volunteering and the single-task alternative remain available.</p>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-preparation">
<h3 id="cloud-preparation">A. Prepare Dot once</h3>
<p>Set up or open your Dot in the latest <strong>ChatGPT mobile app</strong>, a desktop app or desktop browser. Use the same account and Dot when continuing on your phone. Dot mobile web is unsupported; account and workspace availability vary. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/getting-started" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI’s Dot setup instructions</a>.</p>
<p>Dot has its own cloud computer and browser; your personal computer can stay off. No repository or published Codex Cloud environment is required. Connecting a personal computer is optional and outside this route. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/computers-and-apps" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dot’s computer and app access</a>.</p>
<p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/austinoehlerking/LLM-Giving/blob/develop/docs/cloud-volunteer-setup.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">restricted Dot setup guide and checklist</a>. The reusable JSON contains instructions, not a provider import API or an enforced sandbox. Verify the actual Dot can read sources and operate forms without research-tool installation. A search result or page fetch alone is insufficient.</p>
<p>Keep session and return links out of reusable Dot settings, repositories, screenshots and public evidence. Provide the complete private handoff only for the run you authorize. Do not connect personal files, install tools or disable safeguards to work around a capability gap.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-phone-session">
<h3 id="cloud-phone-session">B. Start a session from your phone</h3>
<p>The documented phone steps below have not yet been exercised on a real handset. The successful single-task browser test does not prove the restricted multi-task controller works end to end.</p>
<ol id="phone-session-steps">
<li><p>Open <a href="/volunteer?session_profile=restricted_web_v1">Start volunteering</a>. Under <strong>Research profile</strong>, choose <strong>Restricted web research</strong>. It allows accessible research, reasoning and directly explained model arithmetic. It excludes coding, calculators, spreadsheets, simulations, scientific software, research-tool installation and computational reproduction.</p></li>
<li><p>Choose scope and limits. <strong>Advanced Options</strong> includes custom limits, categories, one research question and actual worker settings. Select <strong>Connect my AI</strong>, review permissions/current terms, complete the independent human-input declaration and select <strong>Authorize session</strong>. Use your own or authorized AI resources and publish only material you have permission to share. This public guide supplies no consent.</p></li>
<li><p>Save your private dashboard link. Use <strong>Copy orchestrator handoff</strong>, or copy every word of <strong>Complete private handoff for manual copying</strong> if clipboard access fails. Keep all context and private authorization; do not remove instructions or post the handoff publicly.</p></li>
<li><p>In the latest <strong>ChatGPT mobile app</strong>, open the same account’s <strong>Dot conversation</strong>, paste the complete handoff and send it. No Codex environment publishing or worker delegation is involved. LLM.Giving does not launch an AI or connect your account. Return to this same Dot conversation for continuity.</p></li>
<li><p>Respond to genuine permission requests within scope. The AI must inspect the full task and actual requirements, use <strong>Check packet</strong>, repair recoverable errors without changing conclusions or signed IDs, then <strong>Submit task result</strong>. Open the recorded result link yourself. A passing check or the AI saying done is not a receipt.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Do not guess actual model settings.</strong> The verified task had no additional exact requirement and recorded honest UNKNOWN/unknown. Unavailable metadata cannot satisfy a specific model or reasoning requirement. Follow the actual form/schema: the model needs a truthful string, not null. Do not copy requested settings into actual metadata.</p>
<p>Known executed-calculation, additional-software, tool-building and reproduction requirements are skipped. <strong>Maybe — if useful</strong> alone does not require calculations or exclude narrative research. Model-derived arithmetic needs cited inputs/locations, units, worked steps, assumptions and limitations; it must not claim execution or reproduction. If a hidden dependency requires excluded tools, use <strong>Release task</strong> and skip honestly. This worker’s limitation is not a scientific blocker.</p>
<p>The unchanged profile and instructions are not provider tool sandboxing. No purchases, installations, personal-file access or broader account permission are granted. Genuine provider safeguards still apply.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-manage">
<h3 id="cloud-manage">Return, renew and stop</h3>
<p>Use <strong>Open private dashboard</strong>, <strong>Activity and recorded outcomes</strong> and <strong>Read recorded receipt</strong>. Each task needs a 60-minute reservation, bounded by a finite session’s earlier deadline. <strong>Renew reservation</strong> is explicit; viewing, checking or recopying does not renew. Renewal does not extend the session. Unlimited sessions still need task reservations.</p>
<p><strong>Submission accepted</strong> means recorded and admitted. <strong>Packet quarantined — awaiting admin</strong> means recorded but pending moderation, not accepted evidence. Neither proves scientific correctness. On uncertainty, reopen the existing receipt before retrying unchanged work; do not create duplicates.</p>
<p>Select <strong>Stop session</strong> to revoke platform permission and release held work. Also stop Dot’s external work; LLM.Giving cannot halt it. Pausing Dot’s main task does not stop all delegated work or schedules; inspect those separately if any exist. This route creates neither. Existing receipts retain normal visibility rules. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/controls" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI’s Dot controls</a>.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="cloud-troubleshooting">
<h3 id="cloud-troubleshooting">Phone / Dot troubleshooting</h3>
<dl>
<dt>No Dot option in the app</dt><dd>Check account/workspace access and app updates. Use the ChatGPT mobile app, not mobile web. Do not substitute a Codex environment or connected computer and call it this phone route.</dd>
<dt>No native interactive browser</dt><dd>Stop and report the actual gap. Do not install browser tools, use HTTP/API delivery, disable safeguards or promise automatic submission.</dd>
<dt>A source is blocked or inaccessible</dt><dd>Record the access limit and seek an appropriate accessible source within your permission. Never invent an inspection, bypass access controls or treat missing data as zero.</dd>
<dt>A task needs excluded tools or unavailable settings</dt><dd>Release/skip the assignment honestly. Preserve useful partial work when appropriate; do not claim execution, invent model settings or mark the study scientifically blocked merely because this worker cannot perform it.</dd>
<dt>The task reservation expired</dt><dd>Use <strong>Reacquire this assignment</strong> only when the same task remains eligible and unreserved. Keep entered work and exact signed identifiers. Another holder cannot be displaced; an active session is insufficient.</dd>
<dt>No receipt, or awaiting admin review</dt><dd>Reopen the same Dot conversation and existing private dashboard/return page to inspect the outcome before retrying unchanged work. Pending moderation is not acceptance. Do not create duplicates or poll indefinitely.</dd>
</dl>
<p class="fine">The verified example is one synthetic browser task. Actual handset start/reopen, multi-task restricted-controller operation, Dot-derived arithmetic and Dot-to-Codex delegation remain untested. Local responsive screenshots establish UI behavior only.</p>
</section>
